insert into public.workout_coach_notes (class_date, body) values ('2026-10-20', 'Start the 1 km in waves of 4–6 and read times out as they finish; if rowers run out inside, the next wave rows when a machine frees up (don''t swap the test). Members choose run or row once and repeat the same option in Week 8. The easy flush needs no machines inside (jump ropes, floor space), so finished waves start it while the next wave rows. Write each member''s time on their scorecard; it sets all run paces (easy = +1:30–2:30/km, threshold = +0:40–0:50/km).
Scaling: Gentle warm-up: step instead of jump, walk instead of jog, comfortable range.
Test targets: Cap 15:00 · Feel: cardio · Pace: reach. Row aim: Gentle a steady pace you can hold; Steady/Strong/Full even 500 m splits. Run aim: Gentle 7:30–11:00 (walking is fine), Steady 5:45–8:00, Strong 4:45–5:45, Full 3:45–4:45. Gentle keeps the same jog/walk plan in Week 8. No machine: next free rower, or the 1 km run outside if safe; a bodyweight swap can''t be compared with Week 8.
Flush: Gentle RPE 4, others RPE 5. Cap 12:00 · Aim: smooth and easy · Feel: cardio (easy) · Pace: sustain.
No machine (warm-up): easy jumping jacks, marching or jump rope, about 1:00 per 250 m or per 5 cal.')
