insert into public.workout_coach_notes (class_date, body) values ('2026-12-08', 'Start the 1 km in waves of 4–6 and read times out as they finish; if rowers run out inside, the next wave rows when a machine frees up (don''t swap the test). Members choose run or row once and repeat the same option in Week 8. The easy flush after the test needs no machines inside (jump ropes, floor space), so finished waves start it while the next wave rows. Record each member''s Week 1 vs Week 8 time on their scorecard.
Test targets: Cap 15:00 · Aim: beat Week 1 time on the same machine or route · Feel: cardio · Pace: reach. Gentle run option: jog 1:00 / walk 1:00 or brisk walk, same plan as Week 1. No rower free: next free rower, or the 1 km run outside if safe; a bodyweight swap can''t be compared with Week 1.
Flush targets: Cap 12:00 · RPE 4 Gentle, RPE 5 others · Aim: smooth and easy · Feel: cardio (easy) · Pace: sustain.
Scaling: Gentle warm-up: step instead of jumping, walk instead of jogging, comfortable range.
No machine: warm-up/cool-down machine → jumping jacks, marching or jump rope, ~1:00 per 250 m or 5 cal.')
